Design a circuit that performs a four-input AND operation followed by an inversion. The module takes a 4-bit input vector, A, and first computes the NAND of pairs of bits, then combines the results using further NAND operations to ultimately produce the AND of all four inputs. Finally, it inverts the result to provide the output Y, effectively implementing an AND function using NAND gates followed by an inverter.
