description:
Design a 16-bit wide synchronous register with reset functionality. On a rising clock edge, if the reset signal is high, the output Q is set to zero; otherwise, it captures and holds the value of input D. The register is capable of storing signed values, providing flexibility for applications that require signed data operations.
module top_module(
  clk, reset, D, Q
);

code:
module top_module(
  clk, reset, D, Q
);parameter W = 16;

input clk;
input reset;
input signed [W:0] D;
output signed [W:0] Q;
reg signed [W:0] Q;

  always @ (posedge clk or posedge reset) begin
    if (reset)
      Q = 0;
    else
      Q = D;
  end
endmodule

